## Original Content
A press conference marking the 103rd anniversary of the massacre following the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake was held in Tokyo on Friday, with participants calling for Japan to confront its history and avoid repeating the mistakes of the past.

## Summary
Activists held a press conference in Tokyo to mark the 103rd anniversary of the massacre following the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake, urging Japan to confront its history. The event emphasized learning from past mistakes to avoid repeating them in the future.

## Key Points
- A press conference was held in Tokyo on Friday to commemorate the 103rd anniversary of the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake massacre.
- Participants called on Japan to acknowledge and confront historical events related to the massacre.
- The gathering highlighted the importance of learning from past errors to prevent similar occurrences.


